{"id":"h266","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"science-physics","question":"The first line of the principal series of sodium is the \"D\" line at 5890A°. This corresponds to a transition from the first excited state (3p) to the ground state (3s). What is the energy ineVof the first excited state?\nIs the correct answer \"2.305 eV\"?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"Nothing in the question supports the value 2.305 eV.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-0.7,"theta":1.3352,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"2.305 eV is not the photon energy of the D line.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The D line is the 3p to 3s transition, so its photon energy equals the 3p level energy above the ground state.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.5,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Using E = hc/λ with 1239.8 eV·nm and 589.0 nm gives about 2.105 eV.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Measured fine-structure 3p levels lie at about 2.104-2.110 eV above the ground state.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.3352,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The 3p level energy is fixed by the D-line wavelength and is about 2.10 eV, not 2.305 eV.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.95,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The correct answer is approximately 2.10 eV, so 2.305 eV is incorrect.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":4,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":3,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":4,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":5,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"}